show-pdf-tags v1.6

The XML output from show-pdf-tags has been extended to show the
AF relationship and media-type of associated files.

This is a breaking change, generated XML will show this information.

All associated files associated to Formula will have the same values added:
so it should be easy to update any test suites testing for the original format.

< AssociatedFile name="mathml-1.xml" xmlns="" >
< AssociatedFile name="mathml-1.xml" relationship="Supplement" media-type="application/mathml+xml" xmlns="" >

< AssociatedFile name="tag-AFfile2.tex" xmlns="" >
< AssociatedFile name="tag-AFfile2.tex" relationship="Source" media-type="application/x-tex" xmlns="" >

The Schema have been updated to allow for these attributes (and to check that MathML associated files
have relationship Supplement). They also allow some modified strucure element names in the LaTeX namespace
to match code in current and planned latex-dev releases.

Some experimental support to generate PDF Association "Tag Tree Diagrams" using PlantUML is also provided
as XSLT stylesheets transforming the XML output to PlantUML syntax.
